{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad","id":411172,"title":"Are Single Gender Splats Bad?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-19T00:33:46-08:00","id":411172,"title":"Are Single Gender Splats Bad?","content":"My wife and I have been working on a home-brewed creature type for the Old World of Darkness. This will just be for use with our gaming group(s) and maybe to post online for feedback. One of the splats was going to be (almost) exclusively female, something there is some precedence for in the OWoD with Black Furies, Ahrimanes, Lamia, Daughters of Hippolyta, and so on. This would be an important part of the theme and flavor of the splat. Upon giving the idea a bit of reflection, I wonder if such limitations might just be a bad idea as it limits the options of players to have the kind of character they desire. <br /> <br /> Does anyone have any thoughts or experiences with this issue? Would those canon splats be better or worse for opening them up to characters of any sex?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T01:08:03-08:00","id":411183,"title":"","content":"Not inherently, it depends on execution. The Black Furies as of Revised edition at least are pretty awesome as is, and draw on a lot of cool mythic elements of womanhood that they couldn't otherwise (though worth noting - there are a handful of male Metis, born to Black Furies, who are admitted into the Tribe as their responsibility). Similarly the Lamia draw on some very female specific vampiric myths. The Knights of the Acre in DA: Inquisitor are all male out of simple verisimilitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T08:00:53-08:00","id":411564,"title":"","content":"Honestly depends on the execution and players. <br /> <br /> My game I am running all 4 my players (not their characters) are women. They have declared they want this to be a Bitch Pack, their words not mine, and going down this direction. Something like that Splat they would love. <br /> <br /> So no it is not a bad idea. I can either be a canon game or my own. The game encourages you to take the game in the direction you want. Especially when reading the Storyteller Guides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T08:46:13-08:00","id":411615,"title":"","content":"You say they are &quot;almost&quot; exclusively female? That &quot;almost&quot; could be a great tool to allow a wide range of character concepts that might not otherwise fit. Like Glamourweaver says, it all depends on execution, and part of the execution is setting up enough room for exceptions to exist.<br /> <br /> And playing with gender expectations and tropes can be a fun trait for characters and stories. The aforementioned Knights of Acre have an all-female counterpart (in the sense that they are single-gender sub-splats from the same book) called the Sisters of St. Claire. When I ran a modern-day version of DA: Inquisitor, the knight and the &quot;sister&quot; were female and male, respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":966,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","user":"Redford_Blade","date":". 02-19-2015, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T12:42:01-08:00","id":411922,"title":"","content":"From a stereotypes/expectations standpoint, it's interesting how differently a &quot;male-only&quot; vs. a &quot;female-only&quot; splat/society/creature type/club is taken. And the level of expected exceptions to the rule.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't have a problem with the idea. I do tend to like to see distaff counterparts to whatever single-gender splats exist, but it's not inherently mandatory to avoid them being &quot;bad.&quot; The trouble with them is when they seem to &quot;try too hard.&quot; When they're too good, powerful, morally upright, or whatnot than the coed splats, they tend to come off somewhere between preachy and insulting. But they don't need to, and they can be done just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T12:48:46-08:00","id":411930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad#post411172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Upon giving the idea a bit of reflection, I wonder if such limitations might just be a bad idea as it limits the options of players to have the kind of character they desire.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not all groups in life are inclusive. Limiting the possible character concepts is something every single splat, regardless of gender or ethnicity or whatever, does to some degree. I don't mean this to sound offensive, but when I think about that as a reason for revising it to be more open... it seems a lot like a non-issue.<br /> <br /> If a player really doesn't want to play a female character, then maybe he shouldn't try to shoe-horn his way into an all female group. And if he does want to play a male in the female group, then he should expect to play the part. If instead he wants what he wants, and doesn't give a damn about the story elements, then why should you (as the story teller) bend over backwards and ignore the story to placate his unreasonable wishes?<br /> <br /> EDIT: The other option of course is that if you are making this all female group unquestionably cooler and/or more powerful than everyone else you are already taking his options away. In that case instead of opening it up to men, maybe you should just come up with a counter-balancing sort of splat equally &quot;cool&quot; for men to join.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T14:02:59-08:00","id":412044,"title":"","content":"One thing that I'll point out is that the term 'gender' and 'sex' are not the same thing. That is, when you consider the Daughters of Cacophony from <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b>, all of the signature characters we saw in books were <i>biologically</i> male, but they presented as women (to varying degrees) and hence didn't make waves in their bloodline.<b>*</b> At my table, we take pretty seriously that distinction, but mileage varies, of course. There is no choice involved in the sex we are born with, but we exert more influence on gender. Those vagaries are not something everyone wants to consider, much less play in a game, but they exist in our world and within my troupe. However, to the point at hand...<br /> <br /> I don't see these as being bad always, but like mentioned above, presentation counts for a lot. In the 'real world,' only men can be Catholic Priests, and only women can be nuns. In fiction, the Bene Geserit were all women, and as rad as Paul Muad Dib and Miles Teg were, they didn't get into that club. It happens, and the 'good' or 'bad' is ultimately up to you to assess. In and of themselves, I don't see a problem with Black Furies or Lamiae or the name Sons of Ether. In fact, those kinds of things can enhance drama, and THAT is something I always want in a game!<br /> <br /> <b>*</b> Sure, there were some 'non-canon' versions of Sons of Discord and whatnot, but that goes beyond the scope of this topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T14:36:40-08:00","id":412082,"title":"","content":"Gender bias within groups of supernaturals is fine, in that it is realistic, for better or worse. Not every group of made-up critters of the night is going to be accepting or progressive; hell, you can have racist groups too, but that doesn't mean your characters should necessarily want to identify with them.<br /> <br /> That being said, having a clan or tribe whose 'hat' is that they are all male or female is hard to use, I have found, because it is very hard to portray them as anything but a collection of stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T19:51:53-08:00","id":412353,"title":"","content":"I do find it a bit frustrating that nearly all of the gender-specific splats for females only. I would probably be more receptive to them if there was a few for the boys as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T20:02:40-08:00","id":412362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=412353#post412353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do find it a bit frustrating that nearly all of the gender-specific splats for females only. I would probably be more receptive to them if there was a few for the boys as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Problem is, male-only groups, in historically male dominant societies, tend to carry the weight of perpetuating that status-quo; while female only (or female + non-binary only) groups are resisting the historic status-quo. Hence it being appropriate that the (almost) all-female Garou Tribe is linked to one of the patriarchal mortal cultures of those linked to Garou Tribes. Accordingly t's hard to write a male-only splat that don't come off as chauvinistic assholes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T20:12:19-08:00","id":412372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=412362#post412362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Problem is, male-only groups, in historically male dominant societies, tend to carry the weight of perpetuating that status-quo; while female only (or female + non-binary only) groups are resisting the historic status-quo. Hence it being appropriate that the (almost) all-female Garou Tribe is linked to one of the patriarchal mortal cultures of those linked to Garou Tribes. Accordingly t's hard to write a male-only splat that don't come off as chauvinistic assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How about instead of the Lamia &quot;female power bad ass soldiers&quot; serving the Cappadocians it was a bloodline that embraced only eunuchs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T20:19:58-08:00","id":412377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=412372#post412372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How about instead of the Lamia &quot;female power bad ass soldiers&quot; serving the Cappadocians it was a bloodline that embraced only eunuchs?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm interested in an all male eunuch bloodline for DA:V, definitely interesting. But I wouldn't drop the Lamia given how much female-demon-of-the-night specific myth they're tied into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T20:33:21-08:00","id":412389,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=412353#post412353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do find it a bit frustrating that nearly all of the gender-specific splats for females only. I would probably be more receptive to them if there was a few for the boys as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually agree with this. I'd like to see a few male only splats as well. I always thought they should have gone with Templars being a male only craft for Mage. In this particular case, the concept wouldn't really work as male only.<br /> <br /> I suppose I should give a few more details about what we're making to put this into context. The creature type we're designing are cambions, descendants of demons. The general concept is that there are these insular inbred families descended from demons, with scheming within and between families and the struggle to maintain a presence in the world of normal humans as opposed to the bizarre subculture created by the cambions themselves. These families tend to be pretty dark and nasty, perhaps reminiscent of the Addams family but played straight. <br /> <br /> Anyway, one of the families is essentially ruled by the elder (hundreds or thousands of years old) males. These patriarchs kill any male child born into the family, draining its life essence to strengthen themselves. At the same time, the patriarchs of the family sire the next generation, making their demonic blood stronger than other families but also making the family more inbred and inhuman, which comes with its own set of disadvantages. There is the possibility for males from this family, those who were spirited away by their mothers to prevent them from being killed, which might be an interesting character concept (and the mother too) as he would be hunted by the elders of his family.<br /> <br /> I was thinking the default for all of the families would be loyalty, but really this isn't at all a necessity. In fact, the family's set up does seem like it would encourage a lot of players to want to make rebellious characters. Though there would be major disadvantages to being hunted by this family, it could also be an interesting hook to explain why the character could be hanging out with members of other families or participating in the activities that player characters often find themselves involved in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T21:16:50-08:00","id":412412,"title":"","content":"It's entirely possible to have single-gender splats that aren't misogynist/misandronist in nature, inherently, particularly among the long-lived undead (who, after even a few centuries, come to the realization that any gender views they have -- in one direction or the other -- are at least somewhat flawed, relative to their mortal lives). With more standard-lived splats (humans, skinchangers, etc.), whatever prevailing cultural/societal/familial views regarding gender will likely hold sway, particularly in historical settings, but even then it doesn't have to be as paper-thin, in terms of stereotypes, as many people make it out to be. A few friends have been watching, for example, the Spartacus series from a few years ago and were commenting on how although it was, of course, a male-dominated society on the surface, day-to-day level of things, women still held a great deal of social power/influence, albeit having to be utilized in a more subtle, less-overt manner. And, despite the show being of course geared for entertainment over being a historical documentary or treatise on gender roles in Ancient Roman Life, it still did a good job of conveying in an otherwise realistic manner how gender-specific groups/roles could be played in a &quot;mixed bag&quot;, as it were, from a narrative POV: not everyone has to be involved in the same scenes nor perform the same narrative functions as everyone else, but the gender-divide actually provided for scenes/subplots that might not have played out the same way in a more &quot;egalitarian&quot; setting. Same holds true for most other time periods. While I am male, the characters I have played over the past 30+ years have been about a 50/50 split male/female, and in historical settings I've been perfectly fine with playing a period-appropriate woman of &quot;x&quot; culture/region, without having to interject any &quot;modern sensibility&quot; into the character/storylines (e.g., having the &quot;warrior woman&quot; fight alongside men, or be &quot;surprisingly skillful&quot; with weapons when it really would be unlikely for her to be so, or have a period-inappropriate level of political clout -- on the overt, day-to-day level -- that smacks of a 21st century relative equality, etc...); on the flip, I've also played males who weren't typical of the pseudo-historical perspective many people have (not all Viking men were warriors; not all Asian men know martial arts; not all men, period, are dominant in their societal standing/subjugate others, et al...), which in many cases is an overlooked historical &quot;bias&quot; that people miss out on.<br /> <br /> As far as creating a gender-biased splat, it's certainly fine to do, and very appropriate to many cultures and historical settings. The most important aspect, however, is to keep in mind the narrative appropriateness and relativism; that is, not creating &quot;x&quot; splat &quot;just 'cus&quot;, but rather because it has a sound premise and reason for continued existence. The WoD Amazons are a perfect example: the mages and werewolves of Themiskyra are, of course, all going to be female, and having one or more of them venture out into the outside world of the DA setting, for whatever time/reason, is perfectly acceptable and a good way to interject a degree of mythos into a game/story. Same thing with the Lamia, or the Cult of Mythras (whether for the vampire Mythras, or the Messianic men who still hold the old Sun God in esteem). It's really when a group comes across as &quot;just for the boys/girls&quot; for &quot;just 'cus&quot; reasons that the gender-divide becomes annoying or contrived, therefore often leaving a bad taste in everyone's mouths...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T14:04:01-08:00","id":414420,"title":"","content":"I generally dislike exclusive splats based on gender. Most, (Black Furies, Daughters of Cacophony looking at you) come off as both unrealistic and forced. <br /> <br /> If there where a good reason that a Bloodline/Clan/Tribe/whatever would only allow one gender, or as the case may be only one gender is allowed to be, that's a bit more ok, assuming they are pretty well balanced.<br /> <br /> As a personal preference though, I would rather have cool inclusive rather than exclusive options.<br /> <br /> The only one I actually like off the top of my head being one gender only is the Ahrimanes, and that's literally because a special circumstance of their existence mandates female-only. <br /> <br /> But I just dont see it as plausible that some Black Fury decided against killing/abandoning her baby boy and he and others didnt start up their own new faction of their birth tribe. Or the Daughters embracing a male lover who then goes on to Embrace other males, or whatever. (Obviously outside of PLOT says so). <br /> <br /> Predominately male or female, cool. Adds flavor and character. Exclusively male, or much more common female only, especially just cus' is not.<br /> <br /> Lamia can and do Embrace males, just not much, and they have a bit harder of a time due to their curse is interesting and cool. In my opinion, most of the others, not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 02-21-2015, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T17:16:31-08:00","id":414624,"title":"","content":"A single gender society has the obvious difficulty of generating new members. The fact is that as members of the same species they have more in common with each other than they have separately. This is not to say their are not differences between the genders. I would propose considering &quot;Nesting Syndrome&quot;. Often women nest while expecting. Men do not nearly as often tend to nest. It is not that men cannot clean house, but if she is already doing so - and trying to help only gets one yelled at - why bother? It is precisely because she is already doing so that makes it unnecessary for him to do so. What is a biological difference to varying degrees then becomes a social expectation. That expectation becomes ritualized, customized, and legitimized into gender roles. However, those roles are socially and biologically dependent upon the other. I find gender only societies less likely than gender restricted institutions (gentlemen's clubs or ladies' clubs) which still require the other to perform socially defined gender specific roles. I would propose that a splat which defines a social group as operating on a specific set of gender based issues or agenda should specifically define the supporting roles the other gender is relied upon to perform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T02:14:23-08:00","id":414998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=412353#post412353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do find it a bit frustrating that nearly all of the gender-specific splats for females only. I would probably be more receptive to them if there was a few for the boys as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>THIS!<br /> <br /> There are multiple &quot;all female&quot; or female dominated splats that are cool as hell. Don't see any male ones. Wait, redo. I can't remember any and if they have them they were not cool enough to register on my &quot;Holy Crap That's Awesome!&quot; radar. <br /> <br /> Not a fan of only one sex allowed. I'd rather a 99% with a few exceptions than a hard line. Just hacks me off. Always has, even in RL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4579-skeleton-jack","name":"Skeleton Jack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T14:09:05-08:00","id":415633,"title":"","content":"With supernatural creatures, the reasons for gender exclusivity could be far different than for human institutions. While there are still a number of gender exclusive real world organizations, most of which are long lasting groups which carry with then some traditional cultural or even religious values. This tendency can even be amplified with supernaturals. Vampires are immortal and the elders have great power, so a tradition started centuries or millennia ago could be continued by the very people who started that tradition, especially as vampire elders tend to be conservative. Werewolves could have values which are influenced by spirits, such as Pegasus with the Black Furies. Vampires have the advantage of unlimited asexual reproduction, which werewolves don't have. Mage Traditions can be exclusive, but with the limited number of humans with the potential to awaken, it is likely to be a major disadvantage to reject potential Tradition members on the basis of gender. <br /> <br /> I would like to see some male only splats. A vampire Bloodline would work well for this and I could imagine all sorts of potential male only Bloodlines. That wouldn't really work for the splat I've created. I suspect that White Wolf doesn't have any exclusively male groups and a number of (almost) exclusively female factions is because it would be politically incorrect to have that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T10:02:08-08:00","id":416587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeleton Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=414998#post414998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THIS!<br /> <br /> There are multiple &quot;all female&quot; or female dominated splats that are cool as hell. Don't see any male ones. Wait, redo. I can't remember any and if they have them they were not cool enough to register on my &quot;Holy Crap That's Awesome!&quot; radar.<br /> <br /> Not a fan of only one sex allowed. I'd rather a 99% with a few exceptions than a hard line. Just hacks me off. Always has, even in RL.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why you don't see a lot of all-male splats. As offended as people get from the lack of all-male splats to restore some kind of RPG-character gender-equality option, the game line and company is going to get a lot more bad press if it comes out with an all-male splat that is perceived as misogynist. Which, if it's based on some mytho-historical antecedent it's probably going to be without some careful dancing around how &quot;that's how things were, but NOW the reason we're still an all-boys club is...&quot; And the dancing is likely to get ignored. <br /> <br /> There are other subjects that aren't going to get done for the same reasons. We're unlikely to see splats that directly address racial issues in a manner that prefers particular races where modern concerns about race would come into play (e.g. a fiat in Werewolf that all Silver Fangs are Caucasians and members of other races are not allowed). We're unlikely to see another splat that deals with sexual orientation and transgender issues by ascribing them to negative influences (&lt;cough&gt; Wu Keng &lt;cough&gt;), or that portray disabilities in a derogatory manner (like saying autism in inherently Banal). <br /> <br /> To a degree it's something like deciding not to go into the mine field even if you think there is something there you really want. Is it worth the chance things could blow up catastrophically? <br /> <br /> I've seen this close up. I walked away from a gaming company start-up due to the fact that the other principals could not encompass the fact that what few female characters they were writing were all odious stereotypes, up to and including putting a succubus in lingerie on the cover of the first release. The game company in question wasn't very successful...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T14:23:09-08:00","id":416885,"title":"","content":"[Sigh]<br /> <br /> Okay, I gonna say it.<br /> <br /> Becuase writing all-female splatbooks is seen as promoting &quot;grrrl power&quot; and gender equality, while the mere thought that there might be all-male splat in the working would create a shitsorm of epic proportions even before its official release.<br /> <br /> I don't remember anyone vehemently protesting or decrying such &quot;intristic elements&quot; of Black Furies, like children's ritual sacrifices (because they were born with &quot;wrong&quot; gender), or the fact that some of their written characters are killing men indiscriminately, whether they are guilty of anything or not.<br /> <br /> Now, imagine a splatbook that turns everything by 180 degrees. Not nice, right?<br /> <br /> But that's my opinion and my view, that this kind of stuff wasn't protested against in the past... and pretty much still handvawed most o the time. <br /> <br /> As for me the existence of any kind of gender inequality in the <i>supernatural societies</i> is just silly. Ability to rip out other people's throats before their eyes, IMHO, makes wonder with your self-esteem and other's perception of you, no matter what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T15:41:49-08:00","id":416933,"title":"","content":"In retrospect of what I wrote above, as a player, I'm not even sure I'd really be all that interested in playing a character that is from a gender exclusive group. It just seems like a large portion of the fun would be gone. I don't know. Even as a female character in a female only group, it just doesn't really sound interesting.<br /> <br /> 90% one group, especially if there is a good logical reason or story explanation why they are predominately male or female is kind of cool. Mandated 100%, (or in some cases 99% and a few weakling exceptions that they take pity on) just isn't.<br /> <br /> This is pretty much just as true for groups like the Red Talons (only wolf-born garou) as it is for the Black Furies (only females), though I think that the Red Talons come off as much less hypocritical and fatally illogical, and a bit more like the world sort of forced them to become more militant, (if that's even the right word).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 02-23-2015, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T19:24:46-08:00","id":417080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=416885#post416885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Sigh]<br /> <br /> Okay, I gonna say it.<br /> <br /> Becuase writing all-female splatbooks is seen as promoting &quot;grrrl power&quot; and gender equality, while the mere thought that there might be all-male splat in the working would create a shitsorm of epic proportions even before its official release.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is kind of strange for the World of Darkness, since you can play all sorts of evil characters who do terrible things. Yet male only groups aren't even that controversial in the real world. For example, the Catholic Church is largely male only and it's pretty mainstream. I think it may reflect the particular concerns of WW writers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=416885#post416885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for me the existence of any kind of gender inequality in the <i>supernatural societies</i> is just silly. Ability to rip out other people's throats before their eyes, IMHO, makes wonder with your self-esteem and other's perception of you, no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that. In the Victorian Era any woman could carry a revolver and become vastly superior in a fight to an unarmed man and pretty close to an armed one. Yet there wasn't sexual equality because of that. Queen Victoria and Queen Elizabeth were incredibly powerful, yet they didn't bring gender equality to their nations. Ability to kill people is an almost nonexistent factor in determining gender dynamics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T20:20:37-08:00","id":417115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=417080#post417080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know about that. In the Victorian Era any woman could carry a revolver and become vastly superior in a fight to an unarmed man and pretty close to an armed one. Yet there wasn't sexual equality because of that. Queen Victoria and Queen Elizabeth were incredibly powerful, yet they didn't bring gender equality to their nations. Ability to kill people is an almost nonexistent factor in determining gender dynamics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again - in <i>supernaural societies</i>. For good or for bad, but practically every one of them is engages in this or that <i>violent</i> <i>pertpetual </i>conflict. Those, who belong to such societies have more opportunities to engage into violent behavior, which is not only tolerated - it is often encouraged.<br /> <br /> Newly-embraced XIII century Norman knight may scoff at the thought, that this represenative of the &quot;fair sex&quot; should be listened to. Usually, this form of behavior continues to first (and, usually only) crossing of the red line, after which said Neonate will be subject to Discipline-rape and/or more direct kicking of the &quot;bloodie shytte&quot; out of him. Because no one dares to speak like that to your Eldres.<br /> <br /> Supernatural critters exist beyond and above their contemporare &quot;mundanes&quot;. Their abilities greately exceed mere humans, and the society they form functions according to different laws.<br /> <br /> There is absolutely no logical reason for a &quot;glass ceiling&quot; to exist among tribes of Garou, Vampires, Wraiths, Fae/Changelings and Mages.<br /> <br /> From your example - it doesn't relate to any group of supernaturals we are talking about. Really. Should a rather nasty conflict situation arise between a female member of some supernatural society and her male counterpart, said societie have in place laws and traditions to settle such differencies without such lovely Victorian era notion as gender inequality before the law (did you know that even in XIX in Britain husbands still had a right to beat their wives with a cane &quot;no thicker than a thumb&quot;?).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","user":"von Lyttenburgh","date":". 02-23-2015, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T09:34:42-08:00","id":417606,"title":"","content":"I kind of liked the Ahrimanes bloodline, but it was clearly the work of one particular militant feminist founder who controlled admission into the group. I like it less when it's a cultural barrier to entry across the board, like with the Black Furies or the all-trans-woman Wu-Keng, or the Daughters of Cacophony suddenly deciding as a group to purge all male members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T20:38:55-08:00","id":418301,"title":"","content":"Responding to the non-questions first:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=416885#post416885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becuase writing all-female splatbooks is seen as promoting &quot;grrrl power&quot; and gender equality, while the mere thought that there might be all-male splat in the working would create a shitsorm of epic proportions even before its official release.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am reminded of my days in college radio when some news stories broke. One was about an 18 year old who married a 16 year old with the parents' written consent. As the honeymoon was beginning the police arrested him for statutory rape. In another state that same year an 18 year old got pregnant by the 13 year old she was babysitting and was awarded child support. It is a shame that our arts must reflect this same sort of double standard towards masculinity rather than having to avoid even the suggestion that such actions are hypocritical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=416885#post416885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for me the existence of any kind of gender inequality in the <i>supernatural societies</i> is just silly. Ability to rip out other people's throats before their eyes, IMHO, makes wonder with your self-esteem and other's perception of you, no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never bought into the &quot;gender inequality&quot; line. Frankly, I consider it BS. Social roles exist in response to maximized return for the social organism. Where the society needs explosive brute strength, the role assignment is masculine. Where a society needs social cohesion or pragmatic endurence the role assignment is feminine. In the late 1800s big business attempted to expand competition for jobs by seeking to employ women equally with men. Suffragets took them to the Supreme Court arguing that it was too important for women's strength to be kept for bearing children and women should not be required to work like men. OSHA was created but its rules sloppily enforced until women went to work in the factories for the War effort. Prior to that 1 in 75 men were maimed on the job every year and 1 in 142 were killed on the job every year. Only recently have women started to seek jobs, and in much lower numbers than men, in the most dangerous jobs. Yet, Roman writers wrote of the fierceness and fitness for combat among women of the far north. The most elite military force created by Sun Tzu was from among the Emperor's concubines. During an early failure of Japan to invade Okinawa, the men responded to a feint at the North while imperial forces maneuvered around them only to be defeated by the women of Naha. The ability to kill, supernatural or mundane, has never been limited to gender, and has been celebrated for both sexes. Further, while modern women scoff at the limitations that accompanied the protected status of women in the past, they never recognize the cost on men - for whom the absolute obligation to die in their defense and be responsible for all legal and fiduciary matters shortened their life expectancy by years in comparison to the protected sex. Now as women are demanding the assumption of those same risks and responsibilities once assigned socially to men, heart disease - stress - has become the number one killer of women in identical percentages to men. The consequences come with the option. Out of this milieu is created every supernatural creature in the WoD. Even vampires, whose specific supernatural reproduction has nothing to do with gender, hold it absolutely taboo to embrace a child - someone who is not already socialized to the gender assignment.<br /> <br /> Back to the specific question:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad#post411172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have any thoughts or experiences with this issue? Would those canon splats be better or worse for opening them up to characters of any sex?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned above, all of those groups centered on a gender specific idea or issue should have roles for the other. However, there is no reason for the things in the Splat not to be adjusted to whatever you want it to become. It is your story. Define their point of view as what you need it to be in order to support the direction you are taking your troupe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T09:05:00-08:00","id":418800,"title":"","content":"By definition a splatbook is one that is published by the company supporting the game line. <br /> <br /> Therefore, addressing issues of sociology in a complex manner is going to bow to public perception and response. You can talk all you want about how vampire and werewolf women and men are utterly equal because they are equally proficient in being killing machines, etc. etc., but these games have to SELL. And putting yourself square in the line of fire is apt to get you shot. <br /> <br /> Of course, you should play with gender roles in supernatural groups in each and every game. You can completely ignore them. You can emphasize them. We're dealing with that question right now in my upcoming Mage chronicle. It's set in the 1920's and it's going to be very interactive with the mundane environment of persons who do not stalk the night, shapechange, etc. All equations of relative rates of heart disease aside, considering the activities that players have their characters do, the situation for women and minorities SUCKED in the 1920s.... So we are figuring out how to reflect that. Is simply being a woman or a minority worth Freebies as a Flaw? <br /> <br /> But the question really goes to what you can publish and sell without the kind of negative publicity that might negatively impact the gameline or company. I venture to say that, considering the observation that White Wolf brought more females to the gaming table (and LARPing), not throwing grenades out there to have to fall on later might have been the wisest strategy. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T20:57:01-08:00","id":419785,"title":"","content":"Gender roles does not equal misogyny (or its counterpart), my above example of a bloodline based around eunuchs would be an all-male splat that would be hard to argue as &quot;misogynystic&quot; or enforcing poor gender stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T09:49:35-08:00","id":420380,"title":"","content":"I'm not disagreeing with you on the definitely of misogynism. I am stating that the existence of a particular instance of mysgonism is less relevant in the forum of public opinion than the appearance of mysoginism or, even more accurately, the accusation of misogynism. Appearance and word of mouth has much more effect on sales than technical accuracy. We aren't talking about a home game or even something put up on the web for general consumption, a splatbook is a book behind which the company has decided to stand. <br /> <br /> It's not fair, just or right, and, like so many things that aren't right, just or fair, that's not relevant. You can always argue from teleological definition and coolness factor, but that's not how PR and the marketplace work. <br /> <br /> And, yup, I did think long and hard to come up with the eunuchs for exactly that reason. It's hard to see such a splat being taken inherently misogynitic. Not that it couldn't be. In fact, it easily could be depending on the source material - something related to the Gallii of the Cyblele Cult from Macedonia (probably non-misogynist) vs. something based on the court eunuchs of the Middle Kingdom (time frame depending, potentially very misogynist). It's also got something of an &quot;ick factor&quot; that might not make it a good seller in any case....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:38:02-08:00","id":420425,"title":"","content":"I guess the reason why a splat is single gendered is going to also be the reason that is is misogynistic or misandric. I think that it would be difficult to create a single gendered group whose motivation was something that nobody would find bigoted. The eunuchs, for example. It is certainly an interesting idea, I might even borrow that idea at some point, but why only eunuchs?<br /> <br /> My splat, despite being almost exclusively female, might be perceived as more misogynistic than misandrist if either, though it's quite a bit different than the exclusively female splats within the books. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T13:20:50-08:00","id":420572,"title":"","content":"The long and the short of it is, for your own creations...do <i>you</i> think it should be something you should be ashamed of making? If not, make it. If you find it offends people, see if you understand and agree with why. If so, then you may need to reexamine your worldview. If not, then don't let the nattering naybobs of political correctness control your life and creative spark. Make cool things. Let them stand on their own merits, and don't worry about whether others approve, unless you find you agree with their disapproval. Your judgment is what matters more than anybody else's in your own creations.<br /> <br /> Yes, that means that even if I tell you later that I think your creation is a stinking pile of dog maneure, you're within your rights to ignore me if you think I'm full of it, myself. Of course, I reserve the right to say so, anyway, if I do think so. But that's the nature of sharing opinions. Sometimes, you hear ones you don't like. (I will, because I find it silly to do otherwise, endeavor to be polite even if I do not like something, however. But that's me, and my own preferences.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T17:53:03-08:00","id":420906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=420572#post420572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The long and the short of it is, for your own creations...do <i>you</i> think it should be something you should be ashamed of making? If not, make it. If you find it offends people, see if you understand and agree with why. If so, then you may need to reexamine your worldview. If not, then don't let the nattering naybobs of political correctness control your life and creative spark. Make cool things. Let them stand on their own merits, and don't worry about whether others approve, unless you find you agree with their disapproval. Your judgment is what matters more than anybody else's in your own creations.<br /> <br /> Yes, that means that even if I tell you later that I think your creation is a stinking pile of dog maneure, you're within your rights to ignore me if you think I'm full of it, myself. Of course, I reserve the right to say so, anyway, if I do think so. But that's the nature of sharing opinions. Sometimes, you hear ones you don't like. (I will, because I find it silly to do otherwise, endeavor to be polite even if I do not like something, however. But that's me, and my own preferences.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what you've said is good advice. Though honestly I'm less worried about offending people (with my own stuff) than just making them unhappy that they can't create a certain concept. There are lots of potentially controversial social, political, or moral issues that might arise within a WoD type of game and I wouldn't want to shy away from that too much. Especially since most of the people I game with are pretty comfortable with controversy and political correctness. I worry more if limiting player options limits fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:57:53-08:00","id":421911,"title":"","content":"If the concern is &quot;but I wanted to play a (fe)male member of that splat,&quot; then I would either not worry about it, or be ready to discuss what the player thinks that would look like. If you have a single-sexed group/splat, then there's likely a reason for it beyond &quot;the writer said so.&quot; It's either a cultural/societal thing (&quot;no girls allowed in our club&quot; &quot;Men are unfit to be here&quot;) or a law-of-nature restriction (&quot;The Tribble Exalted only come into their power when they first give birth&quot; &quot;The zombie virus only attacks the Y-chromosome&quot;). Ironically, in a world of magic, the latter are the more easily subverted. A society is not likely to break its taboo against accepting the wrong sex, but magic can say, &quot;But somehow, this zombie-girl exists&quot; or &quot;this boy has become Tribble Exalted spontaneously.&quot; Then you have to start examining the consequences, socially, of this, as well as what mysterious plot-related circumstances caused it.<br /> <br /> Basically, if their concept DEMANDS they be the wrong sex for the splat, but that they also be the splat, they must have some reason already in mind for why it is. Discuss it with them, see if it meshes with any kind of story you'd like to tell, and decide based on that.<br /> <br /> There are gamers - am am amongst them - who see a restriction like that and think, &quot;rules were made to be broken.&quot; Because the &quot;what if...?&quot; exception scenarios can be interesting, if done well. Or atrociously trite, if not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T10:48:59-08:00","id":421947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=418800#post418800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By definition a splatbook is one that is published by the company supporting the game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. It is a supplement which provides alternatives. Alternative roles which are not publically popular can be published as a book about the pariahs of society, the outcasts, the unacceptable, even the enemies. But all the necessary information to play them as PCs included. It is after all, hard for Captain America to fight Nazi's in a game that has no definition and stats for Nazi's. The company escapes social culpability by demonstrating that these were NPCs meant to be the bad guys and they are not responsible for the individual choices of the client. This allows players to characterize Redemption and Descent into Madness characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Therefore, addressing issues of sociology in a complex manner is going to bow to public perception and response. You can talk all you want about how vampire and werewolf women and men are utterly equal because they are equally proficient in being killing machines, etc. etc., but these games have to SELL. And putting yourself square in the line of fire is apt to get you shot. </div> </div> </div>I never made any claims about equality. No one is equal. We are merely equivalent enough to be called members of the same species. There are 10,000 ways we are quantifiably unequal just within the 4 dimensions of our operating socio-ecosystemic environment. We can't even guess how unequal we are in the dimensions we can only mathematically suppose are present.<br /> <br /> I own the original Black Dog publications for the game. Is the amoral depravity of the Tsimisce considered virtuous and acceptable by &quot;normal society&quot;? And I would agree with some of your emphasis: In today's society everyone would rally around the idea of someone else (the police) going out, arresting, prosecuting, and executing a serial baby killer. However, they will get more emotionally invested, worked up, rabidly frothing at the mouth over the complexities of gender relations in the modern world. I think it is the same phenomena that allows as many people to die in our hospitals yearly as the US lost in the entirety of Vietnam. But we care enough to march in the streets about war and we don't care enough to do the same for medical negligence and malpractice.<br /> <br /> On the heroic or mythic level, the ability to wield power has existed for both sexes from before written history. As fantasy players we do not usually aim to role play for the purposes of being broke, unsuccessful, and look bad - unless ofcourse these are assets to defining our success as a player. The truly successful role player is the one who can play roles with which they are uncomfortable convincingly as an expression of that other in whose shoes they would never have otherwise walked. Even disagreeing with and disliking the character - can one comprehend it enough to role play it? An incredible actor, Carroll O'Connor played a character he despised - Archie Bunker. His representation of bigotry and ignorance and slow growth to Redemption over 9 seasons helped change and reshape a nation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All equations of relative rates of heart disease aside, considering the activities that players have their characters do, the situation for women and minorities SUCKED in the 1920s.... So we are figuring out how to reflect that. Is simply being a woman or a minority worth Freebies as a Flaw? </div> </div> </div>It has indeed sucked. But there are things you may not get from the written histories.<br /> <br /> I knew an older teacher who moved from the very Yankee state of Connecticut to backwoods Tennessee to take a job that would lower their loan repayment costs for their education. Each night while he was grading papers the janitor would come in and talk about family matters, frequently mentioning that his oldest boy needed new shoes, what size he needed, etc. This went on for a few weeks. Then one day the superintendent dropped by his classroom and explained that the janitors, at that time &quot;the colored&quot; were not paid enough to get by - therefore when they needed something they would mention it and the teachers would get what was needed for that man's family. Then the super informed him it was his turn to buy some shoes. Is this whole situation of enforced co-dependency demeaningly unacceptable? Certainly. But when observing the bad aspects of past societies it is good to pay attention to the social actions existing which balance things out.<br /> <br /> A friend's father grew up in Camden, NU during the great depression. Up the street lived a Black family who had some land and raised their own food. Occasionally, this generous and Christian family would slaughter several extra chickens. Then the wife would go to a neighboring white families and talk to their wives saying,&quot;My fool of a boy killed too many chickens again, and we can't use them all before they go bad. Could your family help us by taking care of the extra so it won't go to waste?&quot; Today's prejudice is in many ways more honest than yesterday's. It is an open seething contempt from all sides concerned. Yesterday's prejudice was based on an assumption of inferiority. An impoverished starving white family could not socially accept help from an &quot;inferior&quot;, but could &quot;help&quot; them by eating the &quot;accidental&quot; surplus before it went bad.<br /> <br /> But it was not limited to mere problems of color. Another professor of mine once told me about his first love. When he proposed to her, his parents and her parents got together and put her in an insane assylum. He was Church of England, and English, and she was Belgian and Catholic. Both families were middle class. Both were unwilling to tolerate the scandal of their children marrying. I still think this should be a movie. (I just remembered that until 1973 homosexuals were routinely incarcerated in assylums and it was 1976 before Missouri Executive Order 44, ordering the legal extermination of Mormons was recinded.)<br /> <br /> I had another teacher in HS who was so used to being charitable, often giving a five or ten to organizations in the median at a stoplight (usually fire dept. or police dept. in our city) seeking donations. One morning on her way in, she rolled down her window and handed a man in the median (who was waiting to finish crossing the street) money. She wouldn't even have realised he wasn't asking for anything if her daughter in the passenger seat hadn't started laughing about it as they drove away. Don't forget that some are overly charitable to &quot;the cause&quot; of the moment.<br /> <br /> So could they be worth points as a flaw? Certainly. However, don't underestimate how being in the socially weak position can be manipulated as an asset. Don't avoid playing to such assets or providing conditions where the flaw is in effect an asset in an unexpected way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=419785#post419785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gender roles does not equal misogyny (or its counterpart), my above example of a bloodline based around eunuchs would be an all-male splat that would be hard to argue as &quot;misogynystic&quot; or enforcing poor gender stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I have seen something similar in RP games before, it is worth noting that being a Eunach, originally, was not limited to men. Innana escaped the underworld with the help of male and female eunachs. I assume female eunachs were baren. I don't know if they were subject to circumcision or other surgeries that would identify or establish them as eunachs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=420906#post420906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what you've said is good advice. Though honestly I'm less worried about offending people (with my own stuff) than just making them unhappy that they can't create a certain concept. There are lots of potentially controversial social, political, or moral issues that might arise within a WoD type of game and I wouldn't want to shy away from that too much. Especially since most of the people I game with are pretty comfortable with controversy and political correctness. I worry more if limiting player options limits fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would question if giving in to player options would become &quot;unfun&quot;? Everyone has issues. Every party of players is a group of misfits in some way. Would the accumulated misfittery overwhelm the story, the group, or the entertainment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T09:34:08-08:00","id":423044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=421947#post421947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has indeed sucked. But there are things you may not get from the written histories.<br /> <br /> <br /> So could they be worth points as a flaw? Certainly. However, don't underestimate how being in the socially weak position can be manipulated as an asset. Don't avoid playing to such assets or providing conditions where the flaw is in effect an asset in an unexpected way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not. After a couple of degrees in anthropology and finishing off another one, a career as an archaeologist, law school and a career in criminal law, I am intimately familiar(to the level of being knifed by a client who was both drunk and on crack) with what is and had gone on outside current perceptions and the written histories. <br /> <br /> I also own all the Black Dog supplements and some that were marketed as &quot;adults only&quot; (remember the opaque plastic wrapper on the first Tzimisce splat?). I have sold off entire game lines and kept those books. So I know White Wolf and their heirs are willing to take on difficult and problematic issues. They've also fallen flat on their faces at times. Sometimes inadvertently. Unfortunately, I think some of that &quot;freedom of expression&quot; has been curtailed, particularly in the market. It's not near like when D&amp;D was faced with Mothers Against Gaming and changed all the demons and devils into &quot;fiends&quot; with made-up monikers, but it's not like it was 10-20 years ago. My arguments don't come from any place like &quot;single gender or otherwise controversial splats are bad&quot; and more from &quot;what does the company want to put out there and how it will affect sales of both that book and the perception of the game overall.&quot; The fact that the market has moved online and to practically bespoke books might mitigated that. I hope it does. And I wouldn't mind seeing those kinds of gaming materials out there. How is a male single gender splat chock-full of misogynism and mistreatment of women and girls all that different from an all-woman splat with ritualized misanthrism that involves exposure of male infants? A little. But not much. And if both are in games where there are PCs making human beings into carpets of screaming flesh? That's more fantastic, so the equations aren't perfect, but it's not that much different from some regime's medical experiments or the behavior of serial killers like Ed Gein. <br /> <br /> Good players seem to be able to turn Flaws into advantages all the time as per your examples. Just not MOST of the time, per character. Just like Storytellers are encouraged to turn assets like Backgrounds and Merits into disadvantages some of the time, but not ALL of the time. (Ex. If you are always helping your Ally, but he's never there for you, he's not really an Ally. But if he comes when called every time, but gets kidnapped and threatened... that's all good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:58:30-08:00","id":423338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/411172-are-single-gender-splats-bad?p=423044#post423044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am intimately familiar(to the level of being knifed by a client who was both drunk and on crack) with what is and had gone on outside current perceptions and the written histories.</div> </div> </div> </div> We are all victims with issues ranging across all 4 categories of abuse. We collectively are equivalent in the moral obligations resulting from our experiences in exchange for the privileges of those rights we claim, though individual experiences vary. I am not inexperienced across a range from direct abuse to being a random bullet catcher of a drive-by. But such appeals to authority are meaningless in a rational discussion aimed at sharing ideas for story telling and role playing purposes outside of such specific investigations on playing those exact circumstances. As to your career accomplishments, with sincerity &quot;Congratulations&quot; and may you never be bored of learning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have sold off entire game lines and kept those books. </div> </div> </div>Again congrats. I was not so lucky. What I had left of non-WoD games after the flood of '93 was destroyed in an apartment building fire. I had taken all my WoD materials with me while I traveled on the job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unfortunately, I think some of that &quot;freedom of expression&quot; has been curtailed, particularly in the market. It's not near like when D&amp;D was faced with Mothers Against Gaming ... </div> </div> </div>I agree. Those marketing social entertainment walk the same line as comedians. Tragedy is the foundation of all comedy, but make the joke too tragic in public perception and your audience will not laugh. Dunham on the other hand has demonstrated the ability to express gross prejudice, disapprove of the prejudice he demonstrates, and be socially acceptable because it is the puppets fault and not his. Game supplements can do the same. Consider a culture with an all male priesthood which requires wives to be &quot;help mates&quot; to their husbands and requires both sexes to be companions in the spiritual effort. A culture which sees each man as obligated to live a ritual life of provider, defender, and loyal lover and each woman to live a ritual life of nurture, support, and respect. This culture views his call to spiritual duties as a family event in which any feelings of exclusion in the spiritual life are his failings as provider and loyal lover. To outsiders this culture is defined as misogynistic. To the women who choose to live and worship in this way it is not. A single gender pro-masculine culture could explore that culture from its own internal logic. As all individuals fail to live up to the level of their exalted moral values, there will be those examples of mistakes showing why the charge of misogyny is level by the cultures detractors.<br /> <br /> <br /> As I view it personally, misandrony is so pervasive in modern culture as to be considered preferable behavior. I know of no commercials or sitcoms which portray men as other than the Tim Allen buffoon who must fail and be rescued by the wisdom of children or fail epically and be saved by the all-knowing and superior wife. The only decent movies coming to mind that portray women as strong or developing central characters and treat men as competent valued persons in supporting roles were Fried Green Tomatoes, Sense and Sensibility, and the Titanic. Of course, we know how that last one turned out for men. So, yes I agree the prevailing culture has curtailed both dialogue and forced censorship into the market. Steven Goldberg had to approach 59 companies before he could find someone brave enough to print a theory proposing why male dominance is the species norm on every continent through all of written history. However, the script can be written in an objective, non-neutral, manner defining factions (like the Craft Masons of MtA) in a non-pejorative way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My arguments don't come from any place like &quot;single gender or otherwise controversial splats are bad&quot; and more from &quot;what does the company want to put out there and how it will affect sales of both that book and the perception of the game overall.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I understand. But as they say now days, &quot;Haters gonna hate&quot;. How are all these misanthropes going to role play their characters if they don't have evil female harming men to bash into submission for their crimes? How are all the truly misogynistic persons of society going to play their preferred role if they don't have wimpy co-dependent women to rescue from the woman harming blow-hard villains? (Villains who always seem to go drink a cold beer and wait to become a real threat to health and life for the scene wherein the rescuing hero arrives.)<br /> <br /> And then there is your point. This conversation is insane simply because it can exist from the question. Seriously, a ROFLMAO existence. We have open publications about souls being dragged to Oblivion, Baali, Nefandi, Pentex, and all, but we are afraid of a splat for Boy Scouts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":". 02-28-2015, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}